WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.102
- One of the hearings I chaired,

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:05.739
we had testimony from a
guy named Dr. Epstein.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.507
- Oh yeah, I know about it.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.175
- And he's a psychologist,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.778
used to be the editor
of Psychology Today.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:12.979
He's an academic,

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.381
he's by the way,
not a conservative,

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.649
he's a liberal Democrat

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.951
who voted for Hillary Clinton

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:84% position:16%
and openly supported
Hillary Clinton.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.055
And he did empirical research

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
on Google's manipulative
search outcomes.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.194
So it's interesting psychology.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you type in a
search, the auto-correct,

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
the auto fill in not
the auto-correct,

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.435
but what automatically populates

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.404
makes a huge difference.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the first few
stories that come up

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.043
make a huge difference.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
And there was a
dramatic differential

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
between when you typed
in Hillary Clinton,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:84% position:16%
it would auto-populate
good things.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.084
- [Dave] Yeah, all
good things, yeah.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.218
- When you typed
in Donald Trump,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
it would auto-populate
bad things.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the stories
that would come up

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.390
would be predominantly
good stories for Hillary,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.860
predominantly bad
stories for Trump.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.062
And what was interesting

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.097
is Dr. Epstein did the study

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.499
and he concluded that in 2016,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:88% position:13%
Google's deceptive
search outcomes shifted

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.076
2.4 million votes
to Hillary Clinton.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said this as a
Hillary Clinton supporter,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:23.283
but he was horrified,
but he also projected,

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.385
he said in 2015,

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.719
he said, big tech
is getting worse.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.921
It's getting more aggressive.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
They could move as many
as 15 million votes

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.194
to the Democrats in 2020.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I think
it's a huge threat.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.766
(soft upbeat music)

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is the Rubin report.

