00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:84% position:16%
All right, here's
something interesting.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.543
We were talking a minute ago

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:81% position:19%
about how you grew
up in New York.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you know where I started
wearing cowboy boots?

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.449
- Well, I'm gonna guess
New York for some reason,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.851 align:start size:75% position:25%
or maybe Jersey.
- New Jersey.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.785
- Why Jersey,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.620
Jersey, cowboy boots what.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.255
- It's a weird story.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.391
So I grew up in Houston

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.960
and in Houston, but I was,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:88% position:13%
as a sort of junior high
and high school kid,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was kind of a preppy
kid for a while.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.801
Had long hair, had
a spike for a while.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.337
I mean, went through
these different phases,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.339
but I was a city boy.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I didn't wear boots
in school growing up.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.744
And then I went to college
at Princeton in New Jersey

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:35.215
and I was 17 and I
was away from home

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.083
and I just got homesick.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.084
And so I said, all right,

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.319
I'm gonna go buy
a pair of boots.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.187
And it was sort of a
way for a 17 year old

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.223
to kind of hold onto your home.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.457
And so I started wearing boots

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.059
as a freshmen in college

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:46.993
and I've worn them ever since,

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.261
but it took going to New Jersey,

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.796
which is a little ridiculous

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:50.997
to start wearing boots.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.665 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So you were basically
the Texas boots guy

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.933
at Princeton university.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.135
- So I remember I had a car

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.372 align:start size:84% position:16%
that my grandfather
had given me,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.474
it was a '78 Ford Fairmont.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.343
We called it the green balm.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:07.013
And I remember digging
that car out of the snow

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.581
using the heel of my boots,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.949 align:start size:88% position:13%
which by the way
doesn't work very well,

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.051
but really like bad idea.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.420
But as a Texas teenager,
I didn't know anybody.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.756
We got it out, but it was...

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.726
- But here we are.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.661 align:start size:88% position:13%
All right, moving on
from boots for a moment.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
