00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.602
It's abusive and it's dangerous.

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:59.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it's the
single biggest threat

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:03.442 align:start size:97% position:3%
to free speech and democracy
we have in this country.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.414
Because big tech has
become a monopoly,

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:11.250 align:start size:97% position:3%
controlling the instruments
of communication.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.121
And I've chaired multiple
hearings in the Senate

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:17.390
on big tech censorship.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.692
And one of the hearings,

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:22.428
we talked about a document
that Google had prepared

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:24.163
it's called the good sensor.

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:27.300 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they prepared, its
PowerPoint about 50 page long.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:31.604
And it talks about how the
old vision of the internet

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:34.340 align:start size:88% position:13%
was the free speech
laissez-faire internet,

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.542
where people could speak
and say what they wanted.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:37.476
And then it talked about

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.045
the new vision of the internet.

00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:41.147
And this is Google's own words

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:45.117 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the European style
censorship model.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.352 align:start size:81% position:19%
And by the way,
the four companies

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:48.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Google identified
as implementing it

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:51.991
were Google, YouTube,
Facebook and Twitter.

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:54.093
This is a conscious decision

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.828
and the dangers are enormous.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:57.530
So the question is,
how do you fix it?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.998
If it is a problem,

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:01.000 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have a long discussion
about whether it's a problem,

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.637
although they're not
hiding it anymore.

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:08.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, I think most
sane people at this point

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.775
would agree that there,

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:11.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
even people that disagree
with us politically on this,

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:13.746
I think most people realize that

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:16.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
the extraordinary amount
of power is a problem

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:17.216
one way or another.

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:18.217
- So I will,

00:10:19.352 --> 00:10:21.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's interesting the
political debate though,

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:24.190
one of the talking points
at big tech in the left

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.325 align:start size:84% position:16%
is they don't engage
in censorship.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.027
And the reason they say that

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:31.130 align:start size:88% position:13%
is they say, well, there
are no objective data

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.765
that prove we do.

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:34.133
And it's,

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:35.334
there's the old aphorism

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:37.603
of the guy who kills his parents

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:39.005 align:start size:81% position:19%
and then pleads
mercy on the court

00:10:39.005 --> 00:10:40.740
'cause he's an orphan.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.242 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's true, there are
no objective data

00:10:43.242 --> 00:10:45.044 align:start size:84% position:16%
because big tech
controls all the data

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:48.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
and there's zero transparency,
zero accountability.

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:49.815
So you can use anecdotes

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:51.717 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I've gone
through lots and lots

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:53.619
of specific anecdotes,

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.154
but every time you ask big tech

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:56.589
and I've done it in writing,

00:10:56.589 --> 00:11:00.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've done it in hearings,
simple questions.

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:03.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
All right, in the
2018 election cycle,

00:11:03.129 --> 00:11:05.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
how many posts from Republican
candidates for office

00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.167
did you block or shadow ban?

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:10.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
How many posts from Democratic
candidates for office

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:12.605
did you block or shadow ban?

00:11:12.605 --> 00:11:14.006
Their objective
answer's to that.

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:15.975
There is a number

00:11:15.975 --> 00:11:17.877
and they know the number

00:11:17.877 --> 00:11:19.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they refuse to
answer it and then say,

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:20.680
there are no data.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.748
And so how do you fix it?

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:24.850
I think one way to fix it

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
is getting rid of
the special immunity

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:28.287
from liability that big tech has

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:29.622
that Congress gave them.

00:11:29.622 --> 00:11:32.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So that's 230, right?
- That's 230.

00:11:32.091 --> 00:11:34.593
And the reason 230 was passed,

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:38.631
Congress believed
big tech would be

00:11:38.631 --> 00:11:40.533
a neutral public forum.

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:42.902
In other words,

00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:45.371
it wasn't fair to sue Facebook

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:50.076
for a comment made by
an individual commenter

00:11:50.076 --> 00:11:51.677
'cause it wasn't, they
weren't the speaker,

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:52.878
it was someone else.

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:54.980 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that was
Congress's reasoning.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.716
So we're gonna give big tech

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:57.950
this immunity from liability

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.652 align:start size:81% position:19%
because it's third
party speakers

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:02.455
and we want to see
the internet grow.

00:12:02.455 --> 00:12:04.623 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, what's happened is
big tech changed their mind.

00:12:04.623 --> 00:12:06.759
They said, we're
not going to be,

00:12:06.759 --> 00:12:09.729
to use the language of
the Google document,

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.298
the laissez-faire free
speech place anymore,

00:12:12.298 --> 00:12:14.233
we're going to sensor,
well, you know what?

00:12:14.233 --> 00:12:16.802 align:start size:88% position:13%
If they're gonna silence
views they disagree

00:12:16.802 --> 00:12:19.238
and promote views
they agree with

00:12:19.238 --> 00:12:20.539
they don't deserve,

00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:22.775
I don't believe as a
public policy matter,

00:12:22.775 --> 00:12:25.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
a special protection
for liability.

00:12:25.478 --> 00:12:28.080
There's also the antitrust laws.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.516
Google is a monopoly.

00:12:30.516 --> 00:12:34.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
By any measure, big tech
is richer, stronger,

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:36.822
more powerful than AT and T was

00:12:36.822 --> 00:12:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it was broken up
under the antitrust laws.

00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:42.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're bigger than
bigger than US Steel was,

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:43.262
a line from the godfather,

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:44.396
were bigger than US Steel,

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:47.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
well they were
bigger than US Steel.

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:50.336
And that abuse of power,

00:12:52.338 --> 00:12:56.108
so I've also, you wanna
talk about the real,

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:58.644 align:start size:97% position:3%
what the Trump administration
did on section 230

00:12:58.644 --> 00:12:59.879
will be challenged.

00:12:59.879 --> 00:13:01.180
It's at the FCC.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.382
There'll be litigation.

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:04.884
The real bite here

00:13:05.918 --> 00:13:09.255
is federal antitrust litigation,

00:13:09.255 --> 00:13:12.658 line:0%
which I have urged the
president to pursue,

00:13:12.658 --> 00:13:14.059 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I have urged the vice
president pursue,

00:13:14.059 --> 00:13:15.528 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I've urged the attorney
general to pursue,

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:16.762 line:0%
I've urged the chairman

00:13:16.762 --> 00:13:18.297 line:0%
of the Federal Trade
Commission to pursue,

00:13:18.297 --> 00:13:19.665 line:0%
I've urged the White House
chief of staff to pursue,

00:13:19.665 --> 00:13:22.001 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I've urged the White
House Counsel to pursue,

00:13:22.001 --> 00:13:25.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
to force the transparency,
to get the answers

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:28.974
and to stop their naked bias.

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:30.509
- Are you worried though

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:33.179
that as we sit here right
now in the middle of July

00:13:33.179 --> 00:13:35.481 align:start size:88% position:13%
only three, four months
before an election

00:13:35.481 --> 00:13:38.250
that in a certain way that
the ship has already sailed,

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.352
the damage that they've done.

00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:43.322 align:start position:0%
And even if you could get
everything you wanted tomorrow,

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:44.290
pass tomorrow,

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.891
by the time the processes

00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:48.561
and the systems are implemented,

00:13:48.561 --> 00:13:50.696 align:start size:84% position:16%
congratulations, the
elections passed.

00:13:50.696 --> 00:13:53.232
- I am deeply worried about it.

00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:55.701
One at one of the
hearings I chaired,

00:13:55.701 --> 00:14:00.072
we had testimony from a
guy named Dr. Epstein.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:01.740
- Oh yeah, I know about it.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.409
- And he's a psychologist.

00:14:03.409 --> 00:14:06.011 align:start size:88% position:13%
He used to be the editor
of Psychology Today.

00:14:06.011 --> 00:14:07.213
He's an academic.

00:14:07.213 --> 00:14:08.614
He's by the way,
not a conservative,

00:14:08.614 --> 00:14:10.950
he's a liberal Democrat

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.218
who voted for Hillary Clinton

00:14:12.218 --> 00:14:13.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
and openly supported
Hillary Clinton.

00:14:13.919 --> 00:14:16.322
And he did empirical research

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.859 align:start size:88% position:13%
on Google's manipulative
search outcomes.

00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:22.428
So it's interesting psychology.

00:14:22.428 --> 00:14:24.029
When you type in a search,

00:14:24.029 --> 00:14:25.431
the auto-correct,

00:14:25.431 --> 00:14:27.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
the auto-fill in not
the auto-correct,

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
but what automatically
populates,

00:14:29.668 --> 00:14:31.670
makes a huge difference.

00:14:33.973 --> 00:14:36.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the first few
stories that come up,

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.276
make a huge difference.

00:14:37.276 --> 00:14:40.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
And there was a
dramatic differential

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:42.581 align:start size:84% position:16%
between when you typed
in Hillary Clinton,

00:14:42.581 --> 00:14:43.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
it would auto-populate
good things.

00:14:43.949 --> 00:14:45.351
- [Dave] Yeah, all
good things, yeah.

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:46.452
- When you typed
in Donald Trump,

00:14:46.452 --> 00:14:47.753 align:start size:84% position:16%
it would auto-populate
bad things.

00:14:47.753 --> 00:14:49.521 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the stories
that would come up

00:14:49.521 --> 00:14:51.657
would be predominantly
good stories for Hillary,

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:55.127
predominantly bad
stories for Trump.

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:58.430
And what was interesting is
Dr. Epstein did the study

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.766
and he concluded that in 2016,

00:15:00.766 --> 00:15:04.236 align:start size:88% position:13%
Google's deceptive
search outcomes shifted

00:15:07.306 --> 00:15:10.376
2.4 million votes
to Hillary Clinton.

00:15:12.478 --> 00:15:14.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said this as a
Hillary Clinton supporter,

00:15:14.179 --> 00:15:17.549
but he was horrified,
but he also projected,

00:15:17.549 --> 00:15:19.718
he said in 2015,

00:15:19.718 --> 00:15:21.053
he said, big tech
is getting worse.

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:22.254
It's getting more aggressive.

00:15:22.254 --> 00:15:25.758 align:start size:88% position:13%
They could move as many
as 15 million votes

00:15:26.792 --> 00:15:28.427
to the Democrats in 2020.

00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:31.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I think
it's a huge threat.

00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:33.399
- So as a sci-fi guy,

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:34.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
cause I know you're
a sci-fi guy,

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:36.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a certain way,
doesn't it feel like

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:38.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're already in
the dystopian future

00:15:38.837 --> 00:15:40.673
that we're always worried about

00:15:40.673 --> 00:15:42.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
that so many great
movies are about that.

00:15:42.241 --> 00:15:45.844
In a way we're kind
of there already.

00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:49.181
- We are because the
power and ubiquity,

00:15:50.916 --> 00:15:53.218 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, what makes
social media different,

00:15:53.218 --> 00:15:55.721
look, there's all sorts
of biased media outlets.

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:57.723
The New York times is
ridiculously biased,

00:15:57.723 --> 00:15:58.991
but you can pick it up

00:15:58.991 --> 00:16:01.660
and you can say, okay,
this is a partisan rag

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.729
and you can know it.

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:07.266
What is so such a game
changer with social media

00:16:07.266 --> 00:16:09.268
is that it's invisible.

00:16:09.268 --> 00:16:11.236
So if they don't
like what you say,

00:16:11.236 --> 00:16:13.572
you can post and it
just fades into ether

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:16.742
and you don't know,
you have no idea.

00:16:16.742 --> 00:16:17.743
So I've got,

00:16:19.244 --> 00:16:21.480
on Twitter, I think
my personal Twitter,

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.349
I think we've got 3.7
million followers.

00:16:23.349 --> 00:16:24.583
I have no idea to this date.

00:16:24.583 --> 00:16:27.119
I've asked by the way the CEO,

00:16:27.119 --> 00:16:28.487
when I post something,

00:16:28.487 --> 00:16:29.922
what percentage of the people

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:32.658
who've chosen to
follow me see it.

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:34.193
They won't answer.

00:16:34.193 --> 00:16:35.794 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Did you know
that shadow banning

00:16:35.794 --> 00:16:38.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
is actually in the
Twitter terms of service?

00:16:38.197 --> 00:16:40.599 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I have not seen that.
- There's a...

00:16:40.599 --> 00:16:41.533
I'll show it to you after this

00:16:41.533 --> 00:16:42.701
or my guys can maybe pull it up

00:16:42.701 --> 00:16:44.470
and we'll show it right now,

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:45.738
in their terms of service

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:47.306
when they renewed
it on January 1st,

00:16:47.306 --> 00:16:49.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they know
nobody's paying attention,

00:16:49.108 --> 00:16:50.075
it actually says that

00:16:50.075 --> 00:16:51.210
they can throttle accounts

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.811
and not throttle accounts.

00:16:52.811 --> 00:16:53.946
So they're telling us

00:16:53.946 --> 00:16:55.914
in their own terms of service

00:16:55.914 --> 00:16:57.116
that it's in there

00:16:57.116 --> 00:16:58.751
and then the guys get
up on Capitol Hill

00:16:58.751 --> 00:17:00.686
and they tell you
we don't do it.

00:17:00.686 --> 00:17:03.689 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It is, the magnitude
of the power.

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:08.460
And you know, you talk
about dystopian worlds,

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.396
the hard left, and
I'm interested Dave.

00:17:10.396 --> 00:17:13.365
So you used to be
a man of the left

00:17:13.365 --> 00:17:14.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
and--
- Nobody's perfect.

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:16.468
- You're not now.

00:17:16.468 --> 00:17:17.302
Why?

00:17:17.302 --> 00:17:19.605
I'd be interested in...

00:17:19.605 --> 00:17:21.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
- My audience has
heard it many times,

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:24.676 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I'll give you the
bumper sticker version was,

00:17:24.676 --> 00:17:27.246
one day it just hit me

00:17:27.246 --> 00:17:30.315
that it could not
possibly be true

00:17:30.315 --> 00:17:32.684 align:start size:88% position:13%
that everyone I
disagree with is a bigot

00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:34.386
and a racist and a homophobe.

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:36.755
And I know that sounds
almost cliche to say,

00:17:36.755 --> 00:17:40.292
but every argument of the
left came down to that.

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:42.294
And I could not believe

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:44.930
somehow that I was
so morally right

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:47.466
about every position
that I had come to

00:17:47.466 --> 00:17:50.602
and that everyone else
was so ridiculously evil.

00:17:50.602 --> 00:17:52.538 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like it was basically
a math equation

00:17:52.538 --> 00:17:54.606
and I was like, the math
doesn't work here anymore.

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:55.874
It can't be right.

00:17:55.874 --> 00:17:58.210
And then the bizarre
thing that happened,

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.312
and I'm sure four years ago,

00:18:00.312 --> 00:18:02.581
I was saying all sorts of
crazy things about you.

00:18:02.581 --> 00:18:04.083
And I was saying all
sorts of crazy things

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.317
about Rand Paul

00:18:05.317 --> 00:18:06.018
and a bunch of people.
- And only half of that

00:18:06.018 --> 00:18:07.252
were true.

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:09.421
- Exactly, but a bunch of,

00:18:09.421 --> 00:18:13.092
but once you suddenly
look at the other side

00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:15.194
and you go, holy cow,

00:18:15.194 --> 00:18:17.362
these conservatives,
these libertarians,

00:18:17.362 --> 00:18:19.631
they really just want
to get out of your way

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:21.033
in most respects.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:23.936
Once you see that,
it's very welcoming.

00:18:23.936 --> 00:18:25.037
So it's like,

00:18:25.037 --> 00:18:26.371 align:start size:88% position:13%
I know we have
political disagreements.

00:18:26.371 --> 00:18:28.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
We disagree on
abortion, for example.

00:18:28.073 --> 00:18:29.708
And I'm more than happy to
talk about it if you want to,

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:30.809
but I know that you wanna live

00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:32.511
in the same country as me

